course: dictionary
lesson: 1436
title: Carpentry: making things from wood
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Carpentry is the skill of making and fixing things from wood. A carpenter uses saws, hammers and planes to build tables, doors and roof frames. The clue is in the word's job: carpenters work with wood.
explain: The word can also mean the woodwork itself. «The carpentry in the old church» means the wooden parts of that church, such as its carved doors, beams and benches. So when you meet carpentry, ask: is someone doing the work, or is it the finished wood?
explain: Carpentry also appears in sayings. «Hit the nail on the head» means be exactly right. It comes from carpentry, where a hammer strikes a nail exactly on its top and it goes straight in. Try the meaning in the sentence: does "be exactly right" fit? It does.
fact: Carpentry is the skill or job of making and fixing things from wood.
fact: A carpenter makes things such as tables, doors and roof frames.
fact: «Carpentry» can also mean the woodwork itself, as in «the carpentry in the old church».
fact: «Hit the nail on the head» means be exactly right, and it comes from carpentry.
fact: The Gospels say that Joseph and Jesus were carpenters.
exercise: What is carpentry? | Growing plants and flowers in a garden | Painting pictures on paper | *Making and fixing things from wood | Cooking food over a fire
exercise: «The carpentry in the old church» means what? | The bells that ring on Sunday | *The wooden work in the church, such as doors and beams | The stone walls outside | The people who pray in the church
exercise: «Hit the nail on the head» means what? | Be very angry | *Be exactly right | Leave the room quietly | Hit a nail with a hammer
test: Who does carpentry? | *A carpenter who makes tables and doors | A baker who makes bread | A gardener who grows roses
test: Which book says that Joseph and Jesus were carpenters? | A book about the weather | *The Gospels | A book about cooking
exam: In carpentry, what keeps your eyes safe when using tools? | Sunglasses for the beach | A woolly hat | *Safety goggles | A dusty apron
